## std/logica.pengu — the logic: methods on the `bool` primitive.
##
## `logica` dota de métodos a `bool` mediante un bloque `enchanting bool:` que
## expone las conectivas de la lógica clásica (conjunción, disyunción,
## negación, XOR, NAND, NOR, implicación material y bicondicional) y la
## conversión a entero. Todo es **PenguScript puro**: sin `declare`, sin
## `antiquus`, sin C.
##
## ## Alcance
## Los operadores del lenguaje (`and`, `or`, `not`) cubren la mayoría de los
## casos. `logica` añade:
## - las conectivas derivadas que no son operador (`xor`, `nand`, `nor`,
##   `implies`, `iff`),
## - una versión **encadenable** de las básicas (`toggle`, `and_with`,
##   `or_with`),
## - `to_int`, para acumular contadores en un bucle.
##
## ## Nota sobre `implies`
## La implicación material `a implies b` es `(not a) or b`: solo es `false`
## cuando `a` es `true` y `b` es `false`. Para cualquier otro par devuelve
## `true`, incluso con `a` falsa. Es contraintuitiva para quien lee `implies`
## como causalidad; la tabla de verdad está en el docstring del método.
##
## ## Memoria
## Ningún método asigna memoria del heap. No hay nada que liberar con `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## import std.spark
## import std.logica
##
## weave main into int:
##     var ready as bool is true
##     var armed as bool is false
##     var blocked as bool is calling ready.implies with armed
##     if blocked:
##         calling spark.println with "not reached"
##     else:
##         calling spark.println with "ready but not armed"
##     calling spark.println with "{calling ready.to_int}"      # 1
##     return 0
## ```
##
## Con esto queda cerrada la serie de módulos de primitivos: `std.numerus`
## (`Num`), `std.integrum` (`Integrum`), `std.fractio` (`Real`),
## `std.littera` (`char`) y `std.logica` (`bool`).

import std.ward

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Module Version (LANGUAGE.md §19.0: every hand-written std module exports one)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Logica module version.
const LOGICA_VERSION as string is "2.0.0"

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Methods on `bool`
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

enchanting bool:

    # ─── Conversión ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    ## Devuelve `1` si `self` es `true` y `0` si es `false`.
    ##
    ## ## Uso típico
    ## Acumular un contador a partir de predicados:
    ## ```pengu
    ## var count as int is 0
    ## var flag as bool is true
    ## set count is count + calling flag.to_int
    ## ```
    ##
    ## ## Nota de implementación
    ## Se escribe `if self: return 1` y no `return self to int`: el checker
    ## acepta casts que el backend C no sabe emitir (el caso `string -> int`
    ## se corrigió en la Fase 3.4), y un `if` explícito no depende de esa ruta.
    weave to_int into int:
        if self:
            return 1
        return 0

    # ─── Negación ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    ## Devuelve `not self`, en forma encadenable.
    ##
    ## `calling b.toggle` equivale a `not b`, pero se puede componer con otras
    ## llamadas (`calling (calling b.toggle).toggle` no es sintaxis válida: usa
    ## una variable intermedia).
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var b as bool is true
    ## var flipped as bool is calling b.toggle     # false
    ## ```
    weave toggle into bool:
        return not self

    # ─── Conectivas básicas encadenables ─────────────────────────────────

    ## Devuelve `self and other`. Forma encadenable de `and`.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var a as bool is true
    ## var b as bool is false
    ## var r as bool is calling a.and_with with b     # false
    ## ```
    weave and_with with other as bool into bool:
        return self and other

    ## Devuelve `self or other`. Forma encadenable de `or`.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var a as bool is true
    ## var b as bool is false
    ## var r as bool is calling a.or_with with b     # true
    ## ```
    weave or_with with other as bool into bool:
        return self or other

    # ─── Conectivas derivadas ────────────────────────────────────────────

    ## Devuelve el "o exclusivo": `true` si exactamente uno de los dos es
    ## `true`, `false` si coinciden.
    ##
    ## `a.xor b` ≡ `a != b` ≡ `not (a.iff b)`.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var a as bool is true
    ## var b as bool is false
    ## var r as bool is calling a.xor with b     # true
    ## ```
    weave xor with other as bool into bool:
        return self != other

    ## Devuelve el bicondicional ("if and only if"): `true` si ambos operandos
    ## coinciden.
    ##
    ## `a.iff b` ≡ `a == b` ≡ `(a implies b) and (b implies a)`.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var a as bool is true
    ## var b as bool is false
    ## var r as bool is calling a.iff with b     # false
    ## ```
    weave iff with other as bool into bool:
        return self == other

    ## Devuelve `not (self and other)` (NAND). Cualquier compuerta lógica se
    ## puede construir con NAND; aquí se usa cuando el caso natural es "no
    ## ambos".
    ##
    ## `a.nand b` ≡ `not (a.and_with b)`.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var a as bool is true
    ## var b as bool is false
    ## var r as bool is calling a.nand with b     # true
    ## ```
    weave nand with other as bool into bool:
        return not (self and other)

    ## Devuelve `not (self or other)` (NOR). Útil para "ninguno de los dos".
    ##
    ## `a.nor b` ≡ `not (a.or_with b)`.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var a as bool is false
    ## var b as bool is false
    ## var r as bool is calling a.nor with b     # true
    ## ```
    weave nor with other as bool into bool:
        return not (self or other)

    ## Devuelve la **implicación material**: `(not self) or other`.
    ##
    ## Es `false` **solo** cuando `self` es `true` y `other` es `false`. Para
    ## cualquier otro par devuelve `true`.
    ##
    ## ## Tabla de verdad
    ## | `self` | `other` | `self.implies other` |
    ## |---|---|---|
    ## | false | false | true |
    ## | false | true | true |
    ## | true | false | false |
    ## | true | true | true |
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var ready as bool is true
    ## var armed as bool is false
    ## var ok as bool is calling ready.implies with armed     # false
    ## ```
    weave implies with other as bool into bool:
        return (not self) or other

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tests
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Helper de test: falla salvo que `got` sea `true`.
weave _t_true with got as bool into void:
    calling ward.assert_true with got

## Helper de test: falla salvo que `got` sea `false`.
weave _t_false with got as bool into void:
    calling ward.assert_false with got

## Helper de test: igualdad exacta de `int`.
weave _t_int with got as int, want as int into void:
    calling ward.assert_eq_int with got, want

test "to_int maps true to one":
    var t as bool is true
    calling _t_int with (calling t.to_int), 1

test "to_int maps false to zero":
    var f as bool is false
    calling _t_int with (calling f.to_int), 0

test "to_int accumulates a counter":
    var total as int is 0
    var t as bool is true
    var f as bool is false
    set total is total + (calling t.to_int)
    set total is total + (calling f.to_int)
    set total is total + (calling t.to_int)
    calling _t_int with total, 2

test "toggle flips true":
    var t as bool is true
    calling _t_false with (calling t.toggle)

test "toggle flips false":
    var f as bool is false
    calling _t_true with (calling f.toggle)

test "toggle twice is the identity":
    var t as bool is true
    var once as bool is calling t.toggle
    var twice as bool is calling once.toggle
    calling _t_true with twice

test "and_with over the four pairs":
    var t as bool is true
    var f as bool is false
    calling _t_true with (calling t.and_with with t)
    calling _t_false with (calling t.and_with with f)
    calling _t_false with (calling f.and_with with t)
    calling _t_false with (calling f.and_with with f)

test "or_with over the four pairs":
    var t as bool is true
    var f as bool is false
    calling _t_true with (calling t.or_with with t)
    calling _t_true with (calling t.or_with with f)
    calling _t_true with (calling f.or_with with t)
    calling _t_false with (calling f.or_with with f)

test "xor is true exactly when the operands differ":
    var t as bool is true
    var f as bool is false
    calling _t_false with (calling t.xor with t)
    calling _t_true with (calling t.xor with f)
    calling _t_true with (calling f.xor with t)
    calling _t_false with (calling f.xor with f)

test "iff is true exactly when the operands agree":
    var t as bool is true
    var f as bool is false
    calling _t_true with (calling t.iff with t)
    calling _t_false with (calling t.iff with f)
    calling _t_false with (calling f.iff with t)
    calling _t_true with (calling f.iff with f)

test "nand is the negation of and":
    var t as bool is true
    var f as bool is false
    calling _t_false with (calling t.nand with t)
    calling _t_true with (calling t.nand with f)
    calling _t_true with (calling f.nand with t)
    calling _t_true with (calling f.nand with f)

test "nor is the negation of or":
    var t as bool is true
    var f as bool is false
    calling _t_false with (calling t.nor with t)
    calling _t_false with (calling t.nor with f)
    calling _t_false with (calling f.nor with t)
    calling _t_true with (calling f.nor with f)

test "implies is false only for true implies false":
    var t as bool is true
    var f as bool is false
    calling _t_false with (calling t.implies with f)

test "implies is true for the other three pairs":
    var t as bool is true
    var f as bool is false
    calling _t_true with (calling t.implies with t)
    calling _t_true with (calling f.implies with t)
    calling _t_true with (calling f.implies with f)

test "implies equals not-or":
    var t as bool is true
    var f as bool is false
    var impl as bool is calling t.implies with f
    var expected as bool is (not t) or f
    calling _t_true with (impl == expected)

test "implies is reflexive":
    var t as bool is true
    var f as bool is false
    calling _t_true with (calling t.implies with t)
    calling _t_true with (calling f.implies with f)

test "iff equals both implications":
    var t as bool is true
    var f as bool is false
    var ab as bool is calling t.iff with f
    var forward as bool is calling t.implies with f
    var backward as bool is calling f.implies with t
    calling _t_true with (ab == (forward and backward))

test "xor equals not iff":
    var t as bool is true
    var f as bool is false
    var x as bool is calling t.xor with f
    var i as bool is calling t.iff with f
    calling _t_true with (x == (not i))

test "nand equals not and":
    var t as bool is true
    var f as bool is false
    var n as bool is calling t.nand with f
    var a as bool is calling t.and_with with f
    calling _t_true with (n == (not a))

test "nor equals not or":
    var f as bool is false
    var n as bool is calling f.nor with f
    var o as bool is calling f.or_with with f
    calling _t_true with (n == (not o))

test "xor is associative":
    var t as bool is true
    var f as bool is false
    var left as bool is calling t.xor with f
    var left_all as bool is calling left.xor with t
    var right as bool is calling f.xor with t
    var right_all as bool is calling t.xor with right
    calling _t_true with (left_all == right_all)

test "and_with distributes over or_with":
    var t as bool is true
    var f as bool is false
    var left as bool is calling t.and_with with (calling f.or_with with t)
    var a as bool is calling t.and_with with f
    var b as bool is calling t.and_with with t
    var right as bool is calling a.or_with with b
    calling _t_true with (left == right)

test "de morgan: not (a and b) equals (not a) or (not b)":
    var t as bool is true
    var f as bool is false
    var nand_result as bool is calling t.nand with f
    var na as bool is calling t.toggle
    var nb as bool is calling f.toggle
    var or_result as bool is calling na.or_with with nb
    calling _t_true with (nand_result == or_result)

test "the predicates compose into a permission check":
    var is_admin as bool is false
    var is_owner as bool is true
    var is_locked as bool is false
    var unlocked as bool is calling is_locked.toggle
    var owner_ok as bool is calling is_owner.and_with with unlocked
    var allowed as bool is calling is_admin.or_with with owner_ok
    calling _t_true with allowed

test "and_with and or_with are idempotent":
    var t as bool is true
    var f as bool is false
    var and_t as bool is calling t.and_with with t
    var or_f as bool is calling f.or_with with f
    calling _t_true with (and_t == t)
    calling _t_false with (or_f == t)

test "and_with and or_with commute":
    var t as bool is true
    var f as bool is false
    var ab as bool is calling t.and_with with f
    var ba as bool is calling f.and_with with t
    var ao as bool is calling t.or_with with f
    var bo as bool is calling f.or_with with t
    calling _t_true with (ab == ba)
    calling _t_true with (ao == bo)

test "the identity elements behave":
    var t as bool is true
    var f as bool is false
    var and_true as bool is calling t.and_with with t
    var and_false as bool is calling t.and_with with f
    var or_false as bool is calling t.or_with with f
    calling _t_true with (and_true == t)
    calling _t_false with (and_false == t)
    calling _t_true with (or_false == t)
